<exercise xml:id="q-triple-sign-two">
<title>The sign of a second integral</title>
<statement>
<p>
<term>Without calculation</term>, decide whether the integral below is
positive, negative, or zero. The region of integration <m>E</m> is the
region bounded by <m>z=x^2+y^2</m> and
<m>z=1+\sqrt{1-x^2-y^2}</m>. See
<xref ref="fig-triple-paraboloid-sphere"/>.
</p>
<me>
\iiint_E \left(2-x^2-y^2\right) dV
</me>
<ol marker="A.">
<li><p>Positive</p></li>
<li><p>Negative</p></li>
<li><p>Zero</p></li>
</ol>

<sidebyside width="97%">
<image>
<latex-image>
\begin{tikzpicture}
\draw[rounded corners=8pt, draw=gray!55, thick] (0,0) rectangle (15,5);
\node[anchor=north west, text=gray!60, font=\footnotesize\itshape]
  at (0.25,4.75) {workspace};
\end{tikzpicture}
</latex-image>
<shortdescription>Blank workspace for the sign of the integral and its justification.</shortdescription>
</image>
</sidebyside>
</statement>
</exercise>

